// Sources of your own.
//
// The app's header has a panel for this ("Your own sources"): it writes the
// setting through the app's own server into the app's data directory
// (%APPDATA%\streamed-arena\personal-sources.json in the desktop app), so
// this file is only needed when you would rather write it yourself.
//
// Copy this file to `personal-sources.json` (next to the app) and point the
// app at the feeds you want it to host. A source listed for a match replaces
// that match completely: the app serves it and asks nobody else.
//
//   {
//     "matches": {
//       "genoa-vs-lecce": "https://your.host/genoa/index.m3u8"
//     }
//   }
//
// A match can carry a referer and a name of its own:
//
//   {
//     "matches": {
//       "genoa-vs-lecce": {
//         "url": "https://your.host/genoa/index.m3u8",
//         "referer": "https://your.host/",
//         "label": "My own server"
//       }
//     }
//   }
//
// A "default" entry is a fallback rather than a replacement: the feed the app
// can find is used while it works, and the default takes over when it does
// not.
//
//   {
//     "default": "https://your.host/live/index.m3u8",
//     "referer": "https://your.host/",
//     "label": "My feed"
//   }
//
// The same file can be given through the environment:
//
//   ARENA_PERSONAL_SOURCE="https://your.host/live/index.m3u8"
//   ARENA_PERSONAL_SOURCES='{"matches":{"genoa-vs-lecce":"https://..."}}'
//   ARENA_PERSONAL_SOURCES_FILE="C:\path\to\personal-sources.json"
{
  "matches": {},
  "default": "",
  "referer": "",
  "label": ""
}
